  "narrative": {
    "intro": "AmerisourceBergen Drug has $5.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 350,860 awards with an average award size of $15.6K. Obligations fell 26.6% year over year. The Department of Defense accounts for $5.5B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Historical obligations by fiscal year were $2.1B in FY21, $2B in FY22, $4.4B in FY23, $6.1B in FY24, and $7.4B in FY25. The largest markets in FY2026 to date are Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing at $3.7B, Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $1.8B, and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $639K. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Justice are smaller buyers at $639K and $28K respectively. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. This profile highlights scale, buyer concentration, market mix, and the recent year over year decline in obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall 26.6% year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense recorded $5.5B in obligations for FY2026 to date, a level that produces an overall decline. Obligations fell 26.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a rise from $2.1B in FY21 to $7.4B in FY25 before the FY2026 to date figure of $5.5B. Those year-by-year totals frame the recent decline."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and agencies dominate AmerisourceBergen Drug’s federal business?",
        "body": "Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is the largest market at $3.7B in FY2026 to date. Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers follows at $1.8B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing is $639K. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer at $5.5B, while the Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Justice account for $639K and $28K respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
